From ef731f19270c19486abc4599da46b2002025c5fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:29:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the reusable text-edit engine + the multi-line
 text_editor

text_edit_core.hpp (new, public): EditBuffer/TextInputState/is_insertable
moved out of widgets.hpp unchanged in spelling, plus the engine both
fields and any custom field share:
- TextEditHistory: bounded (128 steps / 32 KiB) coalescing undo/redo -
  word runs, held-backspace runs and type-over-selection merge into one
  step; entries carry both spellings and both caret pairs, guarded by
  the buffer lengths they remember (a caller's rewrite voids the
  history instead of corrupting it). Out-of-line in text_edit_core.cpp.
- the word walk (word_start/word_end, VS Code-style stops: words,
  punct runs, spaces skip) and the line walk (line_start/end/count/
  index/start_of) - cluster-aligned, pure (buf,len) functions.

widgets_detail.hpp: the whole editing keyboard spelled ONCE
(text_field_keys) and walked by both fields - caret keys with
Ctrl+Left/Right word steps, Home/End (line bounds multiline, Ctrl =
doc ends), Ctrl+Backspace/Delete word eats, typing through the filter
(word chars coalesce), the clipboard trio as one recorded step,
Ctrl+A, Escape, Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y / Ctrl+Shift+Z. num_input opts out of
the single-line Up/Down->Home/End mapping (its stepper owns them) and
clears the history at every canonical respell.

widgets_text_editor.cpp (new): the multi-line editor - Enter breaks
lines (Ctrl+Enter passes through as the app's submit chord), Up/Down
carry the goal column, Ctrl+Up/Down walk paragraphs, click places by
(line, x), sweeps select, the wheel scrolls and the follow keeps the
caret's line on screen (a same-line caret never fights the wheel),
the IME preedit rides the caret's line, the scrollbar is the scroll
panel's own thumb. Painters row + gallery demo included.

libs/input: kY/kZ join the named keys. test_ui_gui.cpp regains the
preamble a past patch lost (it could not compile); new suite
test_ui_text_edit (14 cases: the walks, the history, the field's new
keys, the editor's vertical half).
